{
  "e7db74e2-02ff-4297-ac9a-860b2bd3c263": {
    "behavior": {
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "voidal-trinket-augur",
          "name": "Augur",
          "type": "activated",
          "costs": [
            { "type": "deplete", "target": "source" }
          ],
          "variableBounds": {
            "x": { "max": 3 }
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "id": "keep",
              "selector": { "controller": "self", "zone": "deck", "fromTop": 3 },
              "count": 1,
              "optional": true
            }
          ],
          "effects": [
            {
              "type": "chooserSelectsTarget",
              "chooser": "opponent",
              "declaration": {
                "id": "detach",
                "selector": { "controller": "opponent", "zone": "play", "type": "resource" },
                "count": { "type": "variable", "id": "x" },
                "optional": true
              },
              "effects": [
                {
                  "type": "forEach",
                  "selected": "detach",
                  "effects": [
                    { "type": "detach", "target": { "type": "selected", "id": "__candidate" } }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "lookAndReorder",
              "player": "controller",
              "count": { "type": "variable", "id": "x" },
              "to": "bottom"
            },
            {
              "type": "if",
              "condition": { "type": "targetExists", "target": { "type": "selected", "id": "keep" } },
              "effects": [
                { "type": "moveCard", "target": { "type": "selected", "id": "keep" }, "to": "deck", "position": "top" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "notes": "AUGUR. Player supplies variables.x (0-3) on activateAbility; variableBounds caps it at 3. 'That opponent may detach up to X resources from their faction' -> opponent-chooser picks up-to-X in-play resources they control, each detached (a face-down obsession/Volition resource or a face-up resource stops feeding the faction). Modeled as an EFFECT rather than part of COST since the engine has no opponent-input-during-cost step; no mechanical difference. 'Look at top X / keep 1 on top / bottom the rest in any order' = Rosy Palmer composition adapted: the kept card is chosen up front (target 'keep'), lookAndReorder(to:bottom, count X) sends the whole top X to the bottom in a player-chosen order, then the kept card is pulled back to the top. Minor deviation: CardSelector.fromTop must be a literal, so 'keep' is picked from the top 3 even when the player chooses X<3 (they see up to 3 cards instead of exactly X). Degenerate X=0 is legal per 'X that is 3 or less' but pointless; not specially blocked."
  },

  "90e8b87e-3c0f-4293-9b51-feb0919c8b18": {
